flowchart TB
    accTitle: Communication — live answers and ordinary API requests
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. The browser uses a live WebSocket connection for chat and HTTP APIs for schema information and other supported requests. The app checks requests and sends progress, SQL, assistant text, and a final response. Invalid requests, lost connections, or timeouts are surfaced as errors. Both hosting adapters share the live-request behavior.
    %% Companion guide: docs/transport-api.md

    BROWSER["Browser or API client"]:::view
    LIVE["Live chat connection: WebSocket: one question per connection"]:::work
    HTTP["HTTP APIs: Schema, AI, SQL, and CSV requests"]:::work
    SERVER["App server: Check and handle the request"]:::work
    STREAM["Live updates: Progress, SQL preview, and answer text"]:::view
    FINAL["Final response: Answer, data, CSV file, or error"]:::view
    ERROR["If invalid, disconnected, or timed out: Show a failure instead of a completed turn"]:::note

    BROWSER -->|1.a. Live chat| LIVE
    LIVE -->|2.a| SERVER
    BROWSER -->|1.b. HTTP request| HTTP
    HTTP -->|2.b| SERVER
    SERVER -->|3| FINAL
    SERVER -->|While working; live chat only| STREAM
    LIVE -.->|Connection fails| ERROR
    SERVER -.->|Request fails| ERROR

